    "body": "The frontend publisher required a product PR’s original head and duplicated a preliminary runtime acceptance, although publication already runs exact-source artifact compatibility. Its browser helper also remained hard-coded to the previous frontend source.\n\nKeep the candidate schema unchanged and admit either the reviewed PR head or its actual canonical main merge. Reuse the successful Node 22/24 source admission while preserving the runtime job’s real policy-skip result. Exact annotated tag, tree, hash and publication-time artifact compatibility checks remain mandatory. The browser helper now selects the accepted source from the registry preserved from the trusted workflow checkout.\n\nAlign actual compatibility to the published Bamboo v2026.10.17 (source 5b317e4e). Assemble the existing isolated provider/browser image from the exact browser-host source and official Linux executable, checking its 245505088-byte length, SHA256 and ELF architecture. No Cargo backend rebuild, new backend release, credentials or permission changes. Product UI files stay frozen at main43e8f420; unrelated open PRs are excluded.\n\nValidation: 248 focused tests passed (source160, browser64, packed acceptance22, binary2), TypeScript and lint passed. Actual Bamboo17 browser compatibility is still pending; the publisher must run it before npm upload. Planned downstream delivery is Bodhi2026.10.26 with only the new frontend lock and CI package pin; Bamboo17 sidecar lock unchanged.",
